From dc83db4c8639ed28ab1111b6478399470d33ead7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "sh.chao" <sh.chao@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 17:28:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Veloce r25-2-0100: batch owned lines and enter proven Darken

Extend the r25-2-0099 format-7 executor without changing its immutable
program representation or painter-order model.

Reuse the immediately preceding exact graphics-state intern entry before
hashing or probing the state table. Repeated CAD state therefore costs one
exact comparison, with no new allocation or semantic approximation.

Replace one CFX_Path construction, render-device dispatch, AGG renderer,
scanline, path-storage, and rasterizer setup per owned two-point line with a
fixed 256-entry stack packet. The AGG driver validates the complete packet
before its first pixel, then rasterizes and composites every line separately
in original order while reusing only immutable setup and bounded scratch.
State, clip, canonical-command, path, Darken, capacity, and cancellation
boundaries flush the packet. Driver rejection replays the same holder ordinals
canonically before continuing.

Permit direct Darken coverage in an outer non-isolated transparency group only
after one allocation-free scan proves the current destination clip is fully
opaque. In that context PDFium's temporary backdrop source-over followed by
Darken is algebraically identical to direct Darken source-over. Transparent,
isolated, nested, printer, Type-3, changed-live-state, and unsupported-device
cases remain canonical at the same ordinal.

This removes measured compilation and execution work without adding a
page-sized cache, candidate allocation, scheduler, lock, JNI/Kotlin policy,
UI-thread work, or second pixel owner.

